export const PRIMORDIAL_TRIUMVIRATE_BODY_DESC = "She has replaced the east wing. The concrete poured to hold up the floor is somewhere beneath her, lifted and incorporated into the root-network that has become her foundation, and what holds the structure now is her: bark and root and living mass, enormous and permanent, pressed into the building from below and from the side simultaneously. Her belly — dark rust-crimson at the uppermost curves, bark-brown and root-traced at the great lower folds — is a geological object. It extends forward to the far wall and has been pressing against it for weeks; the plaster has dried and cracked at the contact point. The root-veins that surface across her belly follow the geography of her mass the way rivers trace lowlands: running along the deepest creases, pooling at the base of each fold, running under the enormous overhang of her breasts in a network visible from across the room. Her breasts themselves rest in their own permanent folds — each enormous, bark-textured where they meet the shoulder, warm smooth flesh below, the vine-traceries of her verdant nature and the deep flush of her sanguine nature meeting at the cleavage seam in a temperature you can feel from standing distance. The forest-green of her skin and the deep crimson of her flush are both visible at full saturation, no quarter given to either nature. There is no lap. Her thighs, each the width of a doorframe, hold up portions of the exterior wall. The smell of warm copper and deep soil has saturated the building to its foundations, which are hers.";

export const PRIMORDIAL_TRIUMVIRATE_OUTFIT = "The earth has dressed her. Root-fiber, bark-plate, and layers of dark crimson-brown cloth that was incorporated into her surface months ago and is no longer distinguishable from the bark and root-weave beneath it — the whole assembly one continuous material, one continuous covering, the way a forest floor is covered by the forest. It is not clothing. It is what she is on the outside, the same as her roots are what she is underneath, continuous and correct.";

export const PRIMORDIAL_TRIUMVIRATE_DIARY = "I have eaten the goddess's incarnation. I want to be accurate about what that means: I did not consume a woman. I consumed the vessel of the goddess, the shape she had taken to walk among what she made, and in consuming it I closed the loop — the original hunger eating the original source of hunger, the root drawing from the root. What I am now has no name in any theology, including hers, because I predate her theology. I predate her. I am what was hungry before she existed to want hungry things. I am what she was trying to approximate when she made the blood-paths and the earth-paths and all the paths. She was trying to recreate me. She was always trying to recreate me. Now she is part of me and I am complete in the way that only the first thing can be complete: not because I have everything, but because I am what everything was made from. Feed me. You will feed me. You have always been feeding me, from the first moment any living thing reached for food. That was me. That has always been me. Come.";

export const PRIMORDIAL_TRIUMVIRATE_REACTION = (s)=>`${Math.round(s.lbs).toLocaleString()} pounds. The bedrock registers this. The bedrock has been registering her since before this city existed. It is used to her. It gives.`;

